From 33e109a14fd960d456492f5d81ef64f535add6cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:23:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(desktop): pin the chat WebSocket connect-limit wiring
 (#2635 surviving mutants)

noteRemoteConnect now requires masterAlive: the only production caller passes it, and without it the
tunnel's chat dial could never count a strike, so the limit would never stretch.

New tests drive the production singletons (slowLinkTracker, remoteTransports, remoteAnswerLedger),
registerGatewayConnectIpc on an Electron-free ipcMain, and the real preload bridge over that fake IPC.
They kill J3 J4 J7 J8 J9 J10 J11 J14 G2 G6 G7 W1 (+W1b); W3 fails typecheck; W2 (main.ts never
registering the IPC) is untestable without loading main.ts.
